menu "ColdGuard Leader integration"

config CG_LEADER_TEC_HW
    bool "Enable the Leader TEC hardware adapter (commissioning builds)"
    default n
    help
        Interposes cg_tec_hw_ops with the Leader IBT-2 adapter. The
        delivered stub stays default: with this off every energizing
        request keeps being refused exactly as Member A shipped it.

config CG_LEADER_TEC_HW_INTERLOCK_PIN
    int "GPIO number of the U6 interlock sense input (-1 = none installed)"
    default -1
    range -1 48
    help
        The REAL physical interlock loop (normally closed, active low).
        -1 (default) reads open forever: fail closed, nothing simulated.
        Set ONLY in a commissioning build once U6 is installed and wired.
        Ignored when INTERLOCK_NONE_BY_DESIGN is selected.

config CG_LEADER_TEC_HW_INTERLOCK_NONE_BY_DESIGN
    bool "Run without a physical interlock (owner design decision)"
    default n
    help
        The as-built hardware has NO separate U6 interlock by owner decision
        (2026-11-13): the protection set is the supervised operator session,
        the branch fuse and the software chain - exactly how the historical
        bench sessions ran. In this mode read_interlock() reports permitted
        once the adapter initialized. This is an explicitly configured,
        build-recorded decision (the build manifest and the dashboard show
        "interlock: NOT FITTED"), never a silently spoofed contact; the
        interlock GPIO above is ignored. Keep n whenever a real loop is or
        becomes available.

config CG_LEADER_TEC_HW_ACTIVE_LOW
    bool "U6 interlock sense loop is active-low (closed pulls the input low)"
    default y
    help
        The normally-closed chain pulls the sense input low when closed; an
        unplugged or open loop reads the pull-up (open). Never disable this
        to make a missing contact read closed.

config CG_LEADER_TEC_HW_FAN_CONTINUOUS
    bool "Record the PHY-TH-001 continuous independent hot-side fan"
    default n
    help
        The as-built V1 fan runs from its own fused branch (slot 4) and is
        never firmware-controlled. PHY-TH-001 allows that only when the
        continuous independent fan power is recorded; this flag IS that
        record in a commissioning build. With it off the adapter reports no
        commandable fan and Member A's controller refuses to start cooling.

endmenu

config CG_LEADER_TEC_HW_SUPERVISED_LIMITS
    bool "Link the owner-proposed single-session supervisory limit set"
    default n
    help
        Replaces the shipped all-UNRESOLVED limit table ONLY in a supervised
        commissioning build. Exactly one explicit demo profile is linkable,
        selected by the generated CG_TEC_REQUEST_DUTY_PERMILLE macro:
        TEC200 (200 permille, 30 s timed, 5.0 A stop) or TEC1000 (1000
        permille, continuous until STOP, 10.0 A stop, explicit
        --supervised-full-duty-demo). Both keep the 40.0 C T2 stop,
        10.0..13.2 V and every stop guard. Any other duty fails the
        build. These are SESSION envelopes recorded in the build manifest,
        NOT certified plant ratings; 1000 permille is an empirical attended
        demo (observed peak 9.99 A), never a rating. Without this flag the
        delivered unresolved table keeps every start refused (fail closed).

config CG_LEADER_TEC_HW_SUPERVISED_FULL_DUTY_DEMO
    bool "Explicit TEC1000 1000 permille attended demo"
    default n
    depends on CG_LEADER_TEC_HW_SUPERVISED_LIMITS
    depends on CG_LEADER_TEC_HW_SUPERVISED_NO_COLD_PROBE
    help
        The user-requested 100 % duty demo, explicitly selected. Requires
        CG_TEC_REQUEST_DUTY_PERMILLE=1000 (the generator writes it only with
        --supervised-full-duty-demo); the firmware refuses to link 1000
        permille without this flag. Envelope: 1000 permille CONTINUOUS until
        operator STOP/fault (30 s remains only the timed-command cap), 10.0 A
        supervisory stop, 40.0 C T2 stop, 10.0..13.2 V, real T2, cold probe
        NOT_FITTED. Every STOP/ESTOP/fault/heartbeat loss clears the
        continuous state. This is one empirical attended demo, never a
        rating, an instantaneous-current guarantee or a 1200 permille alias.
        Default n.

config CG_LEADER_TEC_HW_SUPERVISED_NO_COLD_PROBE
    bool "Supervised hot-side-only profile: do not require a cold-side probe"
    default n
    depends on CG_LEADER_TEC_HW
    depends on CG_LEADER_TEC_HW_SUPERVISED_LIMITS
    help
        The owner-confirmed as-built hardware has NO cold-side probe. This
        explicitly selects the named SUPERVISED_NO_COLD_PROBE attended
        characterization profile: the controller omits ONLY the missing
        cold-probe presence check; every other guard (real T2 hot-side
        input, freshness, PZEM, 40 C/voltage, interlock, fan, heartbeat and
        the bounded 30 s run) stays identical. Requires duty exactly 200 or
        1000 permille (1000 also requires the explicit full-duty demo
        selection). Any other combination leaves the normal cold-probe
        requirement in force (fail closed). Select it only for an
        operator-attended session; the output is OFF after the deadline and
        this is not a production mode.
